# Classification of every file under overlay/.
#
#   replace  the path MUST already exist in the pinned upstream commit.
#            We are taking ownership of an upstream file. If upstream renames
#            or deletes it, this row fails the build -- otherwise we would go
#            on shipping a dead override that nothing notices.
#
#   new      the path MUST NOT exist in the pinned upstream commit.
#            We are adding a file. If upstream starts shipping one at the same
#            path, this row fails the build -- otherwise a plain copy would
#            silently clobber it.
#
# The distinction is the point. A plain rsync overlay succeeds forever, in
# both of those situations, and tells you nothing.
#
# mode     path

# ── Identity ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# pacman -Q resolves real package names, never `provides`, so every upstream
# command that probes for the `omarchy` package reports nothing on an
# Antharchy system: no version, channel "unknown", and a permanently dark
# SystemUpdate widget in the bar. These are whole-file replacements rather
# than patches because each is a behaviour rewrite; as patches they would
# conflict on any upstream edit to the same file.
replace  bin/omarchy-version
replace  bin/omarchy-version-channel
replace  bin/omarchy-channel-current
replace  bin/omarchy-update-available
replace  bin/omarchy-channel-set
replace  bin/omarchy-update-keyring

# ── CLI aliases ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Symlinks, matching how upstream ships its own bin/ symlinks.
new      bin/antharchy
new      bin/antharchy-version

# The pinned-source model means the dev channel cannot link the overlay repo
# directly; this materializes a tree first. Referenced by omarchy-channel-set.
new      bin/antharchy-dev-checkout

# ── Package channels ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# omarchy-refresh-pacman copies these over /etc/pacman.conf wholesale. That is
# only destructive while the templates are upstream's -- once they are ours and
# carry [antharchy], the command is correct as written and is left unpatched.
#
# These currently describe the aarch64 repo set (Arch Linux ARM, no multilib,
# no [omarchy]). Per-architecture generation lands with the PKGBUILDs in
# Phase 2; see docs/overlay.md.
replace  default/pacman/pacman-stable.conf
replace  default/pacman/pacman-rc.conf
replace  default/pacman/pacman-edge.conf
replace  default/pacman/mirrorlist-stable
replace  default/pacman/mirrorlist-rc
replace  default/pacman/mirrorlist-edge

# ── Branding ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# antharchy-settings seeds logo.txt and icon.txt into /etc/skel as the
# screensaver and About art, so replacing them here rebrands both surfaces
# with no runtime work.
#
# icon.txt is 24-bit TrueColor ANSI half-block art rendered at a terminal cell
# aspect ratio of 0.395. The generator that produced it was never committed --
# see branding/tools/README.md.
replace  logo.txt
replace  icon.txt
replace  icon.png

# NOTE: logo.svg is deliberately absent. It is still upstream's Omarchy
# wordmark and we have no Antharchy replacement yet; listing it here with
# upstream's own content would be an override that claims to change something
# and does not. Outstanding content work.

# ── Version ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstream's `version` file reads 4.0.0.alpha at every commit on quattro -- it
# is a dev marker, not a release number. Ours is derived from upstream.lock so
# there is one version number in the project.
replace  version

# ── Applications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Replacing the 37signals web apps removed in delete.list.
#
# NOTE: both reference Icon=claude and no such icon file exists yet, so they
# render with a fallback icon. Outstanding content work.
new      applications/Claude.desktop
new      applications/Anthropic Console.desktop

# ── Antharchy-owned tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Upstream's version-, channel- and update-available-tests assert upstream's
# package NAMES and its -dev pair, so they cannot pass here by construction.
# This is the test for the model we actually have.
new      test/antharchy.d/identity-test.sh
